<article class="env-corollary" id="027Y">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/027Y">Corollary <span data-tag="027Y">5.6.3.3</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. Then $U$ is a left covering map (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="022N" href="/tag/022N">4.2.3.8</a>) if and only if the following pair of conditions is satisfied: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The induced map $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{U}: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ is a left covering functor (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="01QH" href="/tag/01QH">4.2.3.1</a>). 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The diagram of simplicial sets 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [r] \ar [d]^{U} &amp;  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) \ar [d]^{\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{U} )} \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}) } \]
</div>
<p>
 is a pullback square. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      The sufficiency of conditions $(1)$ and $(2)$ follows from Proposition <a data-tag="022W" href="/tag/022W">4.2.3.16</a> and Remark <a data-tag="022V" href="/tag/022V">4.2.3.15</a>. To prove the converse, assume that $U$ is a left covering map. By virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="027X" href="/tag/027X">5.2.7.4</a>, we may assume that $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}= \int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F}$ for some morphism of simplicial sets $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{Set})$. Let us abuse notation by identifying $\mathscr {F}$ with a functor from the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ to the category of sets. Using Proposition <a data-tag="0275" href="/tag/0275">5.6.3.2</a>, we can identify $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}$ with the category of elements $\int _{\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}} \mathscr {F}$ of Construction <a data-tag="01Q8" href="/tag/01Q8">5.2.6.1</a>. Condition $(1)$ now follows from Remark <a data-tag="01QP" href="/tag/01QP">5.2.6.9</a>, and condition $(2)$ by combining Example <a data-tag="026R" href="/tag/026R">5.6.2.8</a> with Remark <a data-tag="0271" href="/tag/0271">5.6.2.18</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
